# Windows only (configured by tests/CMakeLists.txt): Catch2's test discovery
# with the test list decoded as UTF-8. On Windows execute_process decodes a
# program's output with the console's code page unless told otherwise, which
# turns the em dash in several test names into mojibake; CTest then asks the
# test executable for a test case that does not exist. A macro, so the output
# variables land in the caller's scope.
macro(execute_process)
    _execute_process(${ARGV} ENCODING UTF-8)
endmacro()
include("@PROTOST_CATCH_ADD_TESTS_SCRIPT@")
